  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The action of thionyl chloride with white phosphorus produces phosphorus trichloride,&nbsp;sulphur dioxide and sulphur monochloride.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><msub><mi>SOCl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>PCl</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>PCl<sub>3</sub>&nbsp;has a pyramidal shape,in which phosphorus is sp<sup> 3</sup> hybridised.</p></blockquote>",
